  "limitations": [
    "Ping/pong is a client-observed round trip, not one-way transport, Native input application, browser rendering or physical latency.",
    "The candidate explicitly changes the extra lab proxy socket policy; old network cohorts are preserved and are not relabelled.",
    "No inference that Nagle exclusively caused previous navigation or expired inputs.",
    "Scheduling and TCP packetization are not frozen by a netem seed.",
    "Socket policy is established by exact source and Node API call, not an independent kernel getsockopt read.",
    "Extra or duplicate application pongs were not logged. All requested IDs completed; this is not a complete receive transcript.",
    "IDs increase across cohorts, making some baseline payloads one or two bytes shorter; the cohorts ran sequentially with fresh connections.",
    "Configured added delay is not a measured Internet SLO. This Node ping path does not measure browser rendering, exact Native input ACK or physical display.",
    "Earlier setup attempts produced no ping measurements; their failure records remain separate.",
    "Historical matrices retain their original proxy-policy/source binding and are not combined with this new policy."
